# Documentation

Every completed feature or significant change must include concise documentation.

Documentation should include:
- Purpose of the feature
- High-level implementation overview
- Architecture decisions
- API endpoints added or modified
- Database or schema changes
- Configuration or environment variable changes
- Dependencies introduced
- Known limitations
- Future improvements where applicable

Keep documentation concise, structured, and easy for another developer to understand.
